 personal  event happened everyone on set knew  humiliation in social  death starts properly at 8:01 and she  couldn't even go home to change she had  to be on set to work she was crying and  totally embarrassed poor Miley  cosmetic-surgery Disney Channel once  their stars to be perfect and that means  that they control their appearance when  Demi Lovato was cast on Camp Rock she  had an adorable gap between her two  front teeth Disney Channel told her to  fix it so she did it's just for voice I  just wanted to fit in and be popular it  has to be hard to be told as a kid that  you need to fix your smile she wishes  that she hadn't fixed her teeth because  she thought that the gap was cute she  was young when she agreed to have  cosmetic surgery for Disney forced to  compete it may seem like all Disney  Channel stars are BFFs but that's not  always the case and Bella Thorne told  j14 that sometimes they were forced not  to be friends she and zendaya liked each  other when they were co-stars on shake  it up but they were forced to compete it  was always a question of who was better  and that made things awkward they wanted  to love each other she said but Disney  was relying on their competition for the  show hard to escape Disney Channel has  given a ton of celebrities their big  break and most of the stars are grateful  for it but there's a flip side to that  people will always associate them with  the characters they played as kids  Hilary Duff had a really hard time  breaking out of her lizzie mcguire  persona it just makes me nervous seeing  you guys changing and me staying the  same all the time it took a long time  for people to see her as Hillary instead  but these days she's glad for her time  on the Disney Channel body image issues  every team deals with body image issues  to some degree but Disney Channel stars  struggle with it a lot they're  constantly in the spotlight and Disney  makes them look a certain way Miley  Cyrus has talked openly about how being  told to be skinny and blonde messed with  her self-confidence she had to wear a  wig and a ton of makeup  she wasn't allowed to look like herself  that's probably why she's so big in the  body positivity movement under pressure  being a Disney Channel star is a lot of  pressure your role models for millions  of kids Ross Lynch from Austin and Ally  said that people expect you to always be  the perfect angel that did see makes you  out to be it's the least I could do  after you donated so much money for  Ally's charity he said everyone thinks  that they know the real you  Kieran Brar from Jessie said it's  overwhelming especially once people  start recognizing you that is a lot for  a kid to deal with wardrobe drama Disney  is very controlling of the image their  stars have in public they even regulate  what they can wear Bella Thorne got into  a ton of trouble a few years ago for  wearing a bikini  Disney thought the bikini was too  revealing but Bella's mom is the one who  picked it out if her mom thought it was  okay why didn't Disney they almost fired  her all right they told Bella's mom that  if Ella messed up again they would  terminate her contract  yikes never grow up the Disney Channel's  target audience is children and preteens  they want their stars to feel relatable  but that isn't easy when you're an adult  Joe Jonas has talked about how the  acting he did wasn't appealing to him at  all  it was humor meant for 10 year olds and  he was 20 but that sweater looks like a  peacock threw up on it he wasn't allowed  to have an onscreen kiss they made him  shave every day so he looked 16 he was  glad to be done with the Disney Channel  so he could grow up now that you guys  know how challenging it can be to be a  Disney star would you still become one  if you were given the chance let us know  in the comments thanks for watching give  this video a big thumbs up and subscribe  to the things  [Music]

